  Optional model-picker layer for Hybrid HTML Engines, built on the Model Core (model-config-contract v2.1). One axis decides the mode: Lanes vary the model, Panel varies the role. Lanes: pin models as exact parallel lanes, one input through many models. Panel, Full: each panel, stage or role owns one model (per-panel Recent history, reassign popover). Panel, Master: one Master model serves every role, with a Master control in the header, full-width cards stacked vertically and a read-only Served by badge per card. Dual-Run offers both, Master canonical. All modes consume the Core API (config, keys, callModel, callModelPatient, RunScope, runBatch) and never re-implement it. Invoke with /catalog lanes, /catalog panel, /catalog panel master or /catalog panel full, or say "add live model catalog", "pin models as lanes", "per-panel model picker", "one model for every stage". A bare /catalog asks one gate question. Skip for engines that only need the default models.
